{"schemaVersion":1,"slug":"merge-intervals","title":"Merge Intervals","pattern":"Intervals","difficulty":"Medium","leetcode":56,"prompt":"Given a list of intervals, combine every group that overlaps into a single interval and return the result. Intervals that merely touch at an endpoint count as overlapping.","examples":[{"input":"intervals = [[1,3],[2,6],[8,10],[15,18]]","output":"[[1,6],[8,10],[15,18]]","why":"[1,3] and [2,6] overlap, so they become [1,6]."},{"input":"intervals = [[1,4],[4,5]]","output":"[[1,5]]","why":"They touch at 4, which still counts."}],"constraints":["1 <= len(intervals) <= 10^4","start <= end for every interval"],"approaches":[{"id":"sweep","label":"Sort and sweep","complexity":{"time":"O(n log n)","space":"O(n)"},"viz":{"intervals":"intervals","spans":"intervals","out":"intervals","span":"interval"},"layout":{},"source":["def sweep(intervals):","    spans = sorted(intervals, key=lambda s: s[0])","    out = []","    for span in spans:","        if out and span[0] <= out[-1][1]:","            out[-1] = [out[-1][0], max(out[-1][1], span[1])]","        else:","            out.append([span[0], span[1]])","    return out"],"variants":[{"id":"typical","label":"Typical","note":null,"result":[[1,6],[8,10],[15,18]],"steps":[{"line":0,"ops":[["set",["intervals"],[[1,3],[2,6],[8,10],[15,18]]]],"note":null},{"line":1,"ops":[["set",["spans"],[[1,3],[2,6],[8,10],[15,18]]]],"note":"interval we're building must start before it ends, so one pass is enough."},{"line":2,"ops":[["set",["out"],[]]],"note":null},{"line":3,"ops":[["set",["span"],[1,3]]],"note":null},{"line":4,"ops":[],"note":null},{"line":7,"ops":[["set",["out"],[[1,3]]]],"note":"A clean gap. Nothing later can reach back past it, so close and move on."},{"line":3,"ops":[["set",["span",0],2],["set",["span",1],6]],"note":null},{"line":4,"ops":[],"note":null},{"line":5,"ops":[["set",["out",0,1],6]],"note":"Overlaps the last kept interval, so widen that one instead of adding."},{"line":3,"ops":[["se